  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "In a large bowl, mix together chicken, flour, ginger, garlic, onion, red pepper flakes, cumin, garam masala, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and arrange the chicken mixture in a single layer.",
    "Bake for 20-25 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through and lightly charred.",
    "In a large skillet, melt 1 tablespoon of butter over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the breadcrumbs and cook, stirring frequently, for 2-3 minutes or until lightly toasted.",
    "Add the chicken broth and stir to combine.",
    "Bring the mixture to a simmer and cook for 2-3 minutes or until slightly thickened.",
    "Stir in the remaining 1 tablespoon of butter until melted.",
    "Serve the chicken mixture over the breadcrumb mixture and garnish with chopped cilantro, if desired."
  ],
